                <pb facs="0301" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860d.01/24: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-07T22:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1919, 10
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 7, 9.40
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2031. Your 1880, May 6th, midnight. Have to-day telegraphed American Consul,
                    Helsingfors, quoting portions of American Mission’s number 1992, of May 5th, 8
                    p.m., and-instructing him to inform the Finnish Government of the recognition of
                    Finland. Lansing.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
